      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This translation of the poem “Éshet Neürim” by Elḥanan ben Yitsḥaq of Dampierre (d. 1184) was made by Israel Zangwill and first published in his collection of poetry, <tei:hi rend="italic">Blind Children: Poems</tei:hi> (1903), under the title, “Israel as Bride and as Beggar” on page 118. (An earlier translation in German was made by Leopold Zunz in <tei:hi rend="italic">Die synagogale Poesie des Mittelalters</tei:hi> (1855), p. 249.)</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_65677_notes"/>
